  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 1141 AM MST Mon Nov 9 2026\n\nModels and ensemble guidance remain in good agreement through\nthe extended period, with the all guidance trending south with a\nsystem next weekend.\n\nWednesday...a dry cold front will drop south across the Plains\nduring the morning hours, causing a northerly wind shift by mid\nmorning. A few gusts near 25 mph may be possible near the Kansas\nborder through the afternoon. The main impact from the front\nwill be slightly cooler temperatures, with 60s across the\nPlains.\n\nThursday through Sunday...upper level high pressure will rebuild\nacross Colorado for Thursday into Saturday, with continued dry\nweather. Temperatures will warm nicely, with upper 60s to lower\n70s during this period, and overnight lows in the 30s on the\nPlains and 20s across the San Luis Valley. As mentioned above,\nguidance has tended south with an upper trough moving into the\nregion. Current guidance takes the upper wave across northern\nMexico, and keeps southern Colorado dry. NBM guidance has yet to\ncatch up to the rest of the guidance and has low pops over the\nweekend.",
